{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbjournal", "label": "DynamoDbJournal", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Vollstaendig serverless, On-Demand-Kapazitaet by default; die Tabelle wird lazy angelegt und der erste Aufrufer blockiert, bis sie ACTIVE ist (CreateTable kehrt zurueck, waehrend die Tabelle noch CREATING ist).", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbsnapshotstore", "label": "DynamoDbSnapshotStore", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": null, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbdurablestatestore", "label": "DynamoDbDurableStateStore", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Durable-State-CAS ist ein nativer konditionaler Write - PutItem ... attribute_not_exists(pid) zum Anlegen, UpdateItem ... revision = :expected zum Aktualisieren - ohne Transaktion und ohne Ruecklesen. Der Contract, zu dem DynamoDB am besten passt.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_transactwriteitems", "label": "Atomarer Append via TransactWriteItems", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Alle Events gehen in ein einzelnes TransactWriteItems, jedes Put mit ConditionExpression attribute_not_exists(pid). Ein konkurrierender Writer kann keinen partiellen Append gewinnen: die Transaktion ist ganz oder gar nicht. Der vorausgehende Head-Read ist nur eine Optimierung, die den haeufigen veralteten Append zu einer billigen Query statt einer abgelehnten Transaktion macht. Die relationalen Backends und MongoDB lesen erst den Head und schreiben dann - ein Fehler mitten im Batch kann dort ein Teilstueck hinterlassen.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_hundred_item_limit", "label": "Append-Limit von 100 Events", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "DynamoDB erlaubt hoechstens 100 Items in einem TransactWriteItems. Ein groesserer Append wird mit einem klaren Fehler abgelehnt statt in Chunks zerlegt - Chunking wuerde die Atomaritaet brechen, auf der das Concurrency-Modell beruht.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_compaction_marker", "label": "Monoton steigende Kompaktierungs-Marke", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Aktualisiert mit attribute_not_exists(deletedTo) OR deletedTo < :value, also GREATEST als Bedingung formuliert; ein niedrigerer Wert wird abgelehnt, und diese Ablehnung ist das erwartete Ergebnis, kein Fehler.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_persistenceids_scan", "label": "persistenceIds ist ein voller Table-Scan", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "DynamoDB kann Partition Keys nur per Scan aufzaehlen, dieser Aufruf liest also die gesamte Events-Tabelle. Das Framework nutzt ihn nie auf einem Hot Path - er ist fuer Projection-Tooling. Ausserdem fehlt eine indizierte Tag-Query: currentEventsByTag faellt auf den Journal-Scan zurueck, weil ein indizierter Pfad eine zweite, nach Tag geschluesselte Tabelle braeuchte.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbjournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_in_memory_journal", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_transactwriteitems", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbjournal", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_hundred_item_limit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_transactwriteitems", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_compaction_marker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbjournal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_persistenceids_scan", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbjournal", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_transactwriteitems", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_in_memory_journalconcurrencyerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_transactwriteitems", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_mongodb_no_transactions_needed", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_dynamodbdurablestatestore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_durable_state_durablestateactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_dynamodb_persistenceids_scan", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_journals_mongodb_mongoquery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/journals/dynamodb.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}